ected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15254_1986304_1992996"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables users to provide input through the screen by using a finger or a pen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1986304">touch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1992996">სენსორი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15254_276552_1992996"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables users to provide input through the screen by using a finger or a pen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="276552">touch input</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1992996">სენსორი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="15255_14930_1224017"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The standard single-byte character encoding scheme used for text-based data. ASCII uses designated 7-bit or 8-bit number combinations to represent either 128 or 256 possible characters.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="14930">ASCII</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1224017">მ