icalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44494_2504031_2505228"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program capability to take speech audio and convert it to text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2504031">speech-to-text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2505228">წარმოთქმულის გარდაქმნა ტექსტად</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44494_2632881_2505228"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A program capability to take speech audio and convert it to text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2632881">speech to text</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2505228">წარმოთქმულის გარდაქმნა ტექსტად</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44495_2504032_2504366"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The speech-to-text add-in for Outlook, Word, and PowerPoint</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2504032">Office Dictate</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2504366">Office Dictate</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44522_2505239_2511315"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature within the Microsoft Rewards program, similar to the Punchcard experience within Xbox Live Rewards (which is transitioning into Microsoft Rewards). Users complete X, Y, and Z - things like daily quizzes, searches, and offers - to get a certain number of points.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2505239">punch card</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2511315">პერფობარათი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44536_2505315_2577452"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a horizontal resolution of 3840 (or 4096) pixels and vertical resolution of 2160 pixels. Several 4K resolutions exist in the fields of digital television and digital cinematography.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2505315">4K</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2577452">4K</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44537_2505358_2505924"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Office Dictate button that allows users to override the Automatic Punctuation mode so that they can use voice commands (such as comma and period) to create punctuation in their document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2505358">Manual Punctuation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2505924">Manual Punctuation</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44546_2506467_2511313"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A record of all purchases made by a user from an online store or portal.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2506467">order history</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2511313">შეკვეთების ისტორია</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44569_2506611_2511319"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that enables Wi-Fi devices to connect directly, without a router or other mechanism, making it simpler to do things like print, share, sync, and display.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2506611">Wi-Fi Direct</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2511319">Wi-Fi Direct</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44586_2506886_2511310"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An app that enables members of a Language community to provide translation and language-related feedback about features. The app is currently available only for Windows Desktop.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2506886">Language Community app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2511310">ენობრივი საზოგადოების აპი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44587_2506888_2511311"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A request to gather and send language feedback using quests in Feedback Hub and the Language Community app.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2506888">language quest</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2511311">ენობრივი დავალება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4459_148656_1463273"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The slide that stores information about the design template applied, including font styles, placeholder sizes and positions, background design, and color schemes.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="148656">slide master</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1463273">ნიმუშის სლაიდი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44608_2573054_2577456"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The section of the expanded view of the profile card that contains LinkedIn profile information.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2573054">LinkedIn profile in Microsoft</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2577456">LinkedIn პროფილი Microsoft-ში</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44611_2509173_2515073"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Outlook feature that allows users to compose and save a message as a template, and then reuse it when they want to.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2509173">Email templates</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515073">ელფოსტის შაბლონები</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4462_72367_506563"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The core of layered architecture that manages the most basic operations of the operating system and the computer's processor. The kernel schedules different blocks of executing code, called threads, for the processor to keep it as busy as possible and coordinates multiple processors to optimize performance. The kernel also synchronizes activities among Executive-level subcomponents, such as I/O Manager and Process Manager, and handles hardware exceptions and other hardware-dependent functions. The kernel works closely with the hardware abstraction layer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="72367">kernel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="506563">ბირთვი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44646_2897501_3088254"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The cloud service that helps protect your enterprise hybrid environments from multiple types of advanced targeted cyber attacks and insider threats.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2897501">Microsoft Defender for Identity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3088254">Microsoft Defender იდენტურობისთვის</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44647_2513424_2518393"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To take an existing story in the Photos app and generate a new version of that story with edits to content, style, music, and other options.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2513424">remix</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2518393">რემიქსის შექმნა</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44648_2513444_2518394"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Groove Music app, a graphical display that changes colors and shapes on the screen in response to the music that is playing. The user can choose from several different visualizers, which each look different.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2513444">visualizer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2518394">ვიზუალიზატორი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44668_2515502_2518389"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The setting (toggle) on account.microsoft.com/family that, when switched on, requires children to get adult permission for the things they buy in the Windows and Xbox stores — except for what they get with gift cards or money in their Microsoft account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515502">Ask a parent</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2518389">მშობლისთვის თხოვნა</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44669_2515503_2518390"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The capability of Microsoft Defender Advanced Threat Protection, which helps protect the data in the specified folder locations from modification by suspicious or malicious apps.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515503">controlled folder access</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2518390">კონტროლირებული წვდომა საქაღალდეზე</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44670_2515507_2518391"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature in Groove Music that allows the sound in specified frequency bands to be amplified or reduced, in order to adjust the quality and character of the sound.​</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515507">equalizer</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2518391">ეკვალაიზერი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44671_2515527_2558492"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of people who uses or shares a common language or dialect and contributes to language-related activities for Windows features.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515527">Language Community</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2558492">ენობრივი საზოგადოება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44672_2515529_2558493"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A section in the Feedback Hub app where users can organize language-related activities for their Language community.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515529">Language Community tab</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2558493">ენობრივი საზოგადოების გრაფა</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="44676_2515692_2517649"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that generates Office 365 reports using SharePoint on-premises diagnostic and usage logs so that administrators can manage their infrastructure more efficiently.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2515692">SharePoint Insights</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2517649">SharePoint Insights</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="447_51731_506442"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that lists errors that were encountered during an operation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="51731">error log</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="506442">შეცდომის ჟურნალი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="4470_54362_506459"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A format of a file, commonly indicated by its file name extension, and indicates which program the file was created in and can be opened with.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="54362">file type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig