o clip to another.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060428">fade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3064569">მინავლება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53743_3060429_3067337"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Clipchamp, to break assets on the timeline of a video editing project into multiple smaller segments.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060429">cut</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067337">მოჭრა</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53744_3060430_3067340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A transition effect placed at the beginning of a video clip that gradually increases the visibility of the image or the sound of an audio track.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060430">fade in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067340">მინავლება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53744_3060431_3067340"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A transition effect placed at the beginning of a video clip that gradually increases the visibility of the image or the sound of an audio track.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060431">fade-in</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067340">მინავლება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53745_3060432_3067341"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A transition effect placed at the end of a video clip that gradually decreases the visibility of the image or the sound of an audio track.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060432">fade out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067341">განათების მატება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53745_3060433_3067341"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A transition effect placed at the end of a video clip that gradually decreases the visibility of the image or the sound of an audio track.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060433">fade-out</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067341">განათების მატება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53746_3060434_3067342"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Clipchamp, to accommodate an oversized image or video into the height of the frame of an editing project, preserving the full image.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060434">fit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067342">მორგება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53747_3060435_3064570"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Clipchamp, to cover a frame with an image or video so that there are no visible empty spaces horizontal or vertically.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060435">fill</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3064570">შევსება</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53748_3060436_3070699"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In Clipchamp, to divide an asset on the video editing timeline into multiple parts.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060436">split</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3070699">გაყოფა</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53749_3060437_3067352"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Clipchamp feature that places a smaller video/image on top of a larger video/image in a video editing project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060437">picture in picture</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067352">სურათი სურათში</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53749_3060438_3067352"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Clipchamp feature that places a smaller video/image on top of a larger video/image in a video editing project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060438">picture-in-picture</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067352">სურათი სურათში</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53750_3060439_3064559"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Clipchamp that increases or reduces the playback speed of a video or audio track.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060439">Clip speed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3064559">კლიპის სიჩქარე</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53751_3060440_3067348"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of motion text title or graphic that covers the lower region of the video frame, often used in TV broadcasting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060440">lower third</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067348">ქვედა მესამედი</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">GEO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53752_3060639_3061521"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature within Microsoft Teams that enables teachers to quickly create and review math assignments for their students.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060639">Math Progress</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="ka"><ntig><termGrp><term id="306152